WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.750
In 1966, the Cultural Revolution began.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:07.950
The political movement soon swept across the whole country.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:10.752
Walls were plastered with colorful sheets of paper.

00:00:10.752 --> 00:00:14.110
Schools closed one after another, their gates shut tight.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:18.058
Students left the classrooms, and education was interrupted.

00:00:18.058 --> 00:00:21.402
Young people left the cities to live in the countryside.

00:00:21.402 --> 00:00:24.966
Many books and cultural relics were destroyed.

00:00:24.966 --> 00:00:28.360
Ancient buildings were not spared either.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.908
In the empty classrooms, only dust remained.

00:00:31.908 --> 00:00:34.699
Teachers left the podiums they loved.

00:00:34.974 --> 00:00:39.226
Sunlight outside the windows shone on empty seats.

00:00:39.226 --> 00:00:42.768
Many families suffered persecution and upheaval.

00:00:42.768 --> 00:00:46.594
People lived in unease through a long ten years.

00:00:46.594 --> 00:00:49.452
This experience affected an entire generation.

00:00:49.452 --> 00:00:52.253
In 1976, the Cultural Revolution ended.

00:00:52.253 --> 00:00:54.777
Schools reopened, and children returned to the classroom.
